title: Wine Is a Mocker – Wine and Strong Drink
description: The Christian walk, part three: what wine means in scripture, look not upon the wine when it is red, not for kings nor for priests, the fruit of the vine at the Lord's supper, and answering the verses used to defend drinking, from the teachings on wine and strong drink.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-walk-wine.html
highlight: wine

# The third of five decks on the walk (the user's call): the teachings on wine and strong drink, pulled out of
# "Separation from the world" and gathered from across the archive (walk, church, false, christ-ot, law, prophecy).
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.
# Fixed: "debt the Bible teaches" -> "doubt" (17244), "be no among winebibbers" -> "be not" (17276).

=== Introduction
--- Wine Is a Mocker [title]
overline: Doctrine · The walk
heading: Wine Is a Mocker
sub: The walk, part three: wine and strong drink.
refs: Proverbs 20:1; Proverbs 23:31; Proverbs 31:4; Ephesians 5:18
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 17244
--- Not wise
big: Proverbs 20:1 | mark: Wine is a mocker, strong drink is raging
p: Many professing Christians today doubt the Bible teaches against drinking alcohol. Proverbs 20:1 is very clear; it's not wise.
p: A fool makes excuses for their behavior, and the unrighteous selectively use the Bible to justify the deception they've given themselves over to.

=== What wine means
# from 1322, 9176
--- Juice of the vine, fresh or fermented
kicker: What wine means
lead: Wine in the Bible means all juices, fresh or fermented. Most places in the Bible it means freshly squeezed or preserved fruit juice. Some places it means fermented.
p: “They didn't know how to preserve juice until Louis Pasteur!” That's an ignorant lie. They did, with multiple methods, including sulphur, boiling, wax capped bottles.
p: New wine, fresh juice, put into an old, dried out and worn cask, as it begins to ferment will give off gasses, causing the bottle to be ruined and the wine to spill out ([[Luke 5:37-38]]).

# from 15985
--- New wine in the cluster
kicker: What wine means
big: Isaiah 65:8 | mark: As the new wine is found in the cluster
p: This is a parable about God not destroying all of Judah, because out of the line of David would come Christ. It is descriptive, not prescriptive. “One saith” indicates a hypothetical person may say.
p: And “new wine” is fresh squeezed juice. And that is a blessing. Jesus says we will drink it new with Him in His Kingdom.

# from 15768
--- Wines on the lees well refined
kicker: What wine means
big: Isaiah 25:6 | mark: wines on the lees well refined
p: The Hebrew word *shemer* refers to the dregs or lees, and it generally is used in a negative context: Moab *hath settled on his lees* ([[Jeremiah 48:11]]). The refining, the filtering, is the difference. Wines filtered from their lees before fermentation, and frequently refined, were significantly weaker and the alcohol content negligible.
quote: Wine is rendered feeble in strength when it is frequently filtered. The strength or spirit thus being excluded, the wine neither inflames the brain nor infests the mind and passions, and is much more pleasant to drink. | Plutarch (46–120 A.D.)
read: app:doctrine-walk~15768 | Wines on the lees well refined
read: app:doctrine-walk~15985 | New wine found in the cluster
read: app:doctrine-law~9176 | New wine in new bottles

=== Keeping the juice sweet
# from the author's summary of his posts on the history of wine (supplied 2026-11-03), with the studies
# 11934 (Jeremiah 26), 17180 (Proverbs 9) and 11898 (John 2). The author's points, kept as written.
--- Sweet juice all year
kicker: Keeping the juice sweet
lead: In biblical and ancient usage, “wine” (*yayin*, *oinos*, *vinum*, *mustum*) commonly referred to the juice of the grape in any state: freshly squeezed, preserved unfermented, or fermented.
- Fresh, sweet grape juice was regarded as a gift and was regularly available year-round, because ancient people possessed reliable methods to prevent or minimize fermentation.
- Alcoholic fermentation was not inevitable or universal. Multiple practical techniques kept juice sweet and non-intoxicating, or only weakly alcoholic when diluted.
- Drunkenness is a sin. Jesus did not produce or serve intoxicating wine that would make people drunk.

--- How they kept it from fermenting
kicker: Keeping the juice sweet
table: Method | How it was done
tr: **Sulfur** | Burning sulfur inside jars, so the fumes kill wild yeasts before the vessel is sealed.
tr: **Boiling down** | Fresh must boiled to a half, a third or less, a thick concentrate (*defrutum*, *sapa*) that resists fermentation, later reconstituted with water.
tr: **Sealing and cold** | Jars coated and stopped with pitch or beeswax, sunk in a cold pond or wet sand: sweet a year or longer (“semper mustum”).
tr: **Removing the skins** | Yeast lives primarily on the skins. Filtering them out before fermentation can begin.
tr: **Dilution** | Any lightly fermented wine mixed with water, essentially non-alcoholic.
tr: **Cool storage** | Cool caves, underground rooms or buried vessels, to slow or prevent fermentation.
note: Not obscure experiments: described in the agricultural treatises of Cato, Columella and Pliny.

--- Not a nineteenth-century invention
kicker: Keeping the juice sweet
lead: The lie that juice wasn't invented until the 1800s by Welch's is a foolish cope.
p: The custom of the time of Christ was to abstain from consuming fermented wine. Jews were expected to not drink alcohol. Especially in the Passover, where all leaven, including the yeasts that ferment juice, were forbidden.
p: Wisdom's wine is mingled: the fruit of the vine mixed with water, spiced with myrrh, sweetened with honey ([[Proverbs 9:2]] · [[Proverbs 9:5]]). And at Cana, *thou hast kept the good wine until now* ([[John 2:10]]): the fruit of the true vine, under a better testament.
take: Jesus didn't get people inebriated at a wedding. He didn't use booze as a memorial of His blood given in a new testament.
read: app:Jeremiah-26 | Jeremiah 26: wine is not always alcohol
read: app:doctrine-wisdom~17180 | Wisdom's feast and the gospel invitation
read: app:John-2 | John 2: the good wine kept until now

=== Look not thou upon the wine
# from 17276
--- At the last it biteth like a serpent
kicker: Look not thou upon the wine
scripture: Proverbs 23:29-33 | mark: Look not thou upon the wine when it is red; At the last it biteth like a serpent
p: The final passage paints the dark reality of alcohol. It leads to sorrow and woe. Babblings and wounds without cause, from drunken stumbling. Red eyes and hangovers. And the sad reality that those given to wine will seek it again, despite all those negatives.
p: The warning that alcohol causes perverse and lustful thoughts in the heart, lowering inhibitions and standards, leading to greater sin, is an undeniable truth.

# from 14740, 6992 (Lot)
--- Woe to him that giveth his neighbour drink
kicker: Look not thou upon the wine
big: Habakkuk 2:15 | mark: Woe unto him that giveth his neighbour drink
p: This is an allegory for the sins of Babylon, and sound doctrine on drunkenness and the warped and perverse results of it. It is a stark reminder of what alcohol does to people, and the disgusting things that come about from it.
p: Lot, who took strong wine with him when he was practically dragged out of Sodom, in despair drinks to a stupor, and his daughters plan an abomination ([[Genesis 19:32-33]]).

# from 17276
--- Be not among winebibbers
kicker: Look not thou upon the wine
big: Proverbs 23:20-21 | mark: Be not among winebibbers
p: Drunks and the overindulgent come to poverty. There are examples in our own families and opportunities to show the results in our streets.
p: It is important for a young man or woman to hear the truth, even if it is your own sin that you struggle with. Honesty about sin and consequences, how it has affected you personally, can help soften the blow when children realize Mom and Dad aren't perfect.
take: Better to be sober and wise.
read: app:doctrine-walk~17276 | The rod, honest instruction, and wine
read: app:doctrine-walk~17244 | Wine is a mocker
read: app:doctrine-false~14740 | Woe to him that giveth his neighbour drink

=== Not for kings, nor for priests
# from 17431
--- It is not for kings
kicker: Not for kings, nor for priests
scripture: Proverbs 31:4-7 | mark: It is not for kings, O Lemuel, it is not for kings to drink wine; Lest they drink, and forget the law
p: This should be the end of the matter for saved believers. We are princes and heirs, co-heirs with Christ. It is not for us to drink wine or strong drink.
p: The only allowance for drinking alcohol is medicinally, for the perishing. For the dying. And for those with no hope, for the miserable. But we have the hope of Jesus. Those without, who don't know Christ, they drink to forget.

# from 11162
--- Nor for priests
kicker: Not for kings, nor for priests
big: Leviticus 10:9 | mark: Do not drink wine nor strong drink
p: It's a standing command from the Lord for those who are called His priests. We who are saved are of the royal priesthood. We are a Tabernacle of the Spirit of God. As priests and princes, we should abstain from intoxicants. We are called to be sober. To be holy because He is holy.
refs: 1 Peter 2:9; 1 Peter 1:15-16

# from 5803, 17431
--- Not given to wine
kicker: Not for kings, nor for priests
big: 1 Timothy 3:2-3 | mark: sober; Not given to wine
p: These standards for the pastors of a church exist to be the example for all young men. And women as well, *Even so must their wives be grave, not slanderers, sober, faithful in all things* ([[1 Timothy 3:11]]).
p: We may have liberty in Christ, and all things may be lawful, but all things do not edify. We should strive to be men of God, blameless.
read: app:doctrine-walk~17431 | It is not for kings to drink wine
read: app:doctrine-walk~11162 | Kings and priests should not drink wine

=== The cup of the Lord's supper
# from 11092, 1322
--- The fruit of the vine, new
kicker: The cup of the Lord's supper
scripture: Matthew 26:27-29 | mark: I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that day when I drink it new with you
p: Fermentation is prohibited during Passover and the feast that followed. It represents sin throughout the Gospel. The process of yeasts breaking down sugars ([[Exodus 12:19]]).
take: Jesus knew no sin. Juice of the vine, new. Amen.

# from 13712, 6814
--- Christ our passover
kicker: The cup of the Lord's supper
big: 1 Corinthians 5:7-8 | mark: Christ our passover is sacrificed for us
p: The blood of Christ was shed on that hill in Jerusalem, it isn't in a cup of juice or wine. But we remember His covenant made by His literal blood and body. His blood was sprinkled on the Mercy Seat in Heaven, one time. One sacrifice.
p: And Melchizedek, king of Salem, *brought forth bread and wine* to Abram ([[Genesis 14:18]]). A sign that the ordinance of bread and wine, of faith in God as savior, was always about Jesus.
read: app:doctrine-church~11092 | The fruit of the vine and unleavened Passover
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~13712 | Christ our Passover, not a wafer

=== Answering the proof texts
# from 1322, 17431, 15985, 15768, added-numbers-28-2
--- The verses used to defend drinking
kicker: Answering the proof texts
table: The verse | The answer
tr: [[John 2:9-10]] | Would Jesus get people drunken, when the Bible *is* clear that's a sin to even look upon it?
tr: [[Isaiah 65:8]] | A parable of Judah spared for the line of David. New wine in the cluster is fresh juice.
tr: [[Isaiah 25:6]] | Wines on the lees *well refined*: filtered, its strength broken.
tr: [[Numbers 28:7]] | Poured out with the burnt offering, a libation for God. The prohibition against the priests' consumption of strong wine ([[Leviticus 10:9]]) presents a problem for those seeking to use this verse to justify it.
tr: [[Proverbs 31:6]] | Strong drink for him that is ready to perish: for the dying and the miserable, not for kings and princes.
p: Without getting into the cope many professing Christians use to justify their drinking, the plain meaning of the text is undeniable.
read: app:doctrine-walk~1322 | Wine in the Bible and the Lord's supper
read: app:Numbers-28 | Numbers 28: the drink offering

=== Filled with the Spirit
--- Be filled with the Spirit [title]
overline: The walk
heading: Be Filled with the Spirit
big: Ephesians 5:18 | mark: be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit
center: That means not being inebriated and forgetting the law. Not being led away by strange women in our alcoholic haze. Not uttering perverse things. Certainly not profaning Christ Jesus to justify our sinful habits.
big: 1 Thessalonians 5:6 | mark: let us watch and be sober
